WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.190
Grizzly's Hibernation Preparations!

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:40.300
Wow, pandas are amazing.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.120
I guess that's what 
 they do in winter.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.470
Time for foo—

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.350
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.550
Oh, Mr. Handa, 
you came at a good time.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.610
Could you make me some tea?

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:13.620
Jeez, what kind of zoo has pandas
 using heated tables?

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.110
It's okay.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.680
I'll sit under here adorably.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.630
It's <i>not</i> okay!

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.360
It's not! Get out!

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.580
You heard the man, Panda.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.380
Younguns should be 
playing with the tire.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.810
I'm gonna hang out here with the 
heater a little bit longer.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.850
You can't be in there, either, 
Mr. Full-Time Panda!

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.000
What? Really?

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.390
Heated tables are prohibited.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.250
Miss Sasako.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.400
Yes?

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:56.390
When I flap like this,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.090
or when I flap like this...

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.810
Which is cuter?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.940
Could I treat this as 
a take-home quiz?

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.760
An immediate reply would be just fine,

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.590
considering this is supposed to be

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:14.920
idle conversation since I'm bored...

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.460
Then they're both exactly the same.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.070
Oh, I see.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.060
What's wrong, Panda?

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.990
I don't understand Mr. Handa.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.430
What happened?

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:38.360
Well...

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:43.280
He says heated tables aren't 
allowed at the Panda Corner!

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.440
Could I get another café 
mocha, Miss Sasako?

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.790
Listen to me...

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.300
I just wasted my time 
listening to you.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:55.110
Then we can talk about what 
you want, Mr. Penguin.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.750
What were you talking about?

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:02.240
Flapping like this...

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.670
Or flapping like this...

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.280
He was asking which is cuter.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:11.850
That's okay, Miss Sasako. 
We can let that go now.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.790
By the way, where's Polar Bear today?

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.380
He said he was going shopping.

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.190
Shopping?

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.450
It's gotten pretty cold.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:32.880
When are you going to start 
hibernating, Grizzly?

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:37.160
It's more like staying inside for 
winter rather than hibernating.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.740
I've gotta start sometime this week.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:46.640
Zunha 
suggests

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:46.640
Pleasant 
Sleep

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:46.640
Bring high class sleep to your bedroom.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:46.640
Winter's Sleep 
Supply Fair!!

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:51.390
Hey, this pillow looks good. 
It's memory foam.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.900
Actually this magnetic pillow 
might be better for sleeping.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:06.410
Most Popular

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.160
Pillows made with Japanese cypress

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.570
are good for relaxation, too.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.410
Hey, Grizzly.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:07.860
Yeah?

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.450
Let's go eat pudding à la mode.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.900
Later.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.380
I'm gonna be sleeping for a while,

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.460
so the right pillow is important.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.700
Then an ice pillow will work.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.840
Actually, just ice.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.600
I'm not like you.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.860
If I slept on ice, I'd die.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.090
I could also go with the 
buckwheat pillows.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:37.710
Foam beads, huh? Not bad.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.570
What the hell, this is hard.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.170
Hey!

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.670
Hey, is it later yet?

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.440
Don't be so annoying!

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:48.880
What the hell are you, 
a grade schooler?

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:52.050
We'll go eat pudding à la mode later,

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:54.330
so let me just concentrate on 
picking a pillow right now.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.960
Then it'll be your treat, Grizzly.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:01.310
Why the hell do I have to treat you?

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:04.430
All right, fine. Just keep quiet.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.300
Okay.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.100
Shhhh...

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.270
I'm telling you to stop that.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.190
Thanks for the food.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.820
You still haven't decided?

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.210
It's not that easy.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.730
Choosing the right pillow is 
essential for hibernation.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.600
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:36.820
So, can I get seconds?

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:38.040
What the hell for?!

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.450
Then you better come with me 
to the department store.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:45.640
The pillow department 
there is pretty solid.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:48.050
What? Pillows again?

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:50.300
Shut up. You're coming with me.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:55.260
Xmas Corner 
on 3F

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:55.260
Give a special gift
to show your appreciation

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:55.260
You can be the star

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:59.100
All right. The pillows 
are on the sixth floor.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.470
I bet they'll have quite a selection.

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:04.820
Well, this is a department store.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.490
Hey, let's eat some Indian curry.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:10.360
You just ate five 
 puddings à la mode!

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:14.360
I think there are more important

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:17.320
things in life than pillows, Grizzly.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.330
And that Indian curry ain't one of 'em.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.540
Oh, don't you need to buy 
some Christmas presents?

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:26.210
I don't care about an event 
that goes on while I'm asleep.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:28.630
Quit it. 
We're going to the sixth floor.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:31.970
But it's so much fun 
picking out presents.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.500
So, this nori seaweed set and 
this vegetable oil set...

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:36.740
Which do you think is better?

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.520
Those are year-end gifts!

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.020
Grizzly.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.670
What?!

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.060
About the pillows...

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.280
I have an idea.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.280
And?

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.440
Hm?

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:55.510
What's this idea of yours?

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:56.590
Oh.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.610
Curry is great in the summer,

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.620
but it's amazing in winter, too!

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:05.530
I knew it'd be something like that.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:07.680
I was an idiot to let 
you drag me here.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.030
Once you finish that,

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.000
we're going to the sixth 
floor to look at pillows.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.300
But...

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.050
No buts!

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:16.550
You ain't leaving until I buy a pillow!

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.290
It never fails. At times like these,

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:27.350
you end up buying from the first store.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:31.430
The memory foam pillow was good, too.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:34.640
Now I can enjoy a great hibernation.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:36.180
Thanks!

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:41.270
Grizzly.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:42.420
What is it?

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.260
I can still eat a little more.

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:46.310
Shut up.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.380
All that walking around made me tired.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:57.960
See you next spring. Take care.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.970
Yeah, you too.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:03.220
Oh, but with global warming happening

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:06.210
I may not be energetic for long.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:10.720
I can't exactly laugh at that.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.690
Oh, more importantly,

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.110
while you're hibernating,

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:20.440
a meteor may come crashing down
and destroy the Earth.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.310
Don't say something creepy like 
that before I'm about to sleep.

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:28.290
Or rather, save your sleep talk 
 for when you're sleeping.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:35.130
Or while you're sleeping, 
a mouse might bite your ear,

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.220
and your body might change color.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:43.280
We'll match.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.010
That ain't gonna happen.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:50.310
Well, see you again next spring.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:52.360
Yeah, see ya.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.150
See you.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:09.870
Hibernating

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.090
Hibernating

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:32.610
Hello...

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.730
Oh, it's Polar Bear.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.170
I'm having some trouble deciding 
on a Christmas present.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.320
Do you have a minute?

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.080
What are you having trouble with?

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:48.220
Beer or king crab... 
Which do you think is better?

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.170
I already told you...

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.030
Those are year-end gifts!

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:02.890
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.660
Grizzly's Hibernation!

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:08.660
Huh? What's going on?

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.560
And I came all this way.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:15.770
Off
Today

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.920
Are the pandas off today?

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:15.650
Huh?

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:21.190
I guess the pandas aren't here.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:23.300
Huh? But the pandas were here...

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:23.300
Let's go home.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:27.040
Off Today

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:27.040
What?!

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:37.880
Hey! What are you two doing?

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:42.990
Are you sure it's okay to open 
such an expensive bottle?

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.050
Please wake up!

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.520
It's okay.

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:50.300
I can sleep anywhere, so you don't have

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:51.830
to worry about me.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:53.670
That's <i>not</i> okay!

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:56.420
And?

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.070
We were discussing what it'd be like

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.160
to work as if we were relaxing at home,

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.560
so we brought out the futons.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.160
Yup.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.600
I'd be okay with doing 
this part-time job

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.220
seven days a week, Mr. Handa.

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.410
That's <i>not</i> okay!

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.000
Futons are also prohibited!

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:16.970
Miss Sasako.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:17.960
Yes?

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:22.800
I'm thinking of making a hit song, 
so could you listen for a sec?

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.760
Is it okay if I don't 
listen right now?

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:26.760
I'm a little busy.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.720
Then I'll just sing it in my head.

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:40.260
You're depressed again, Panda?

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:46.000
I really don't understand what 
Mr. Handa is thinking anymore.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.450
What happened now?

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.490
You see...

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:53.670
We said we'd like to sleep 
in futons in the office,

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:56.080
but Mr. Handa said we couldn't!

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.680
Could I get another café 
mocha, Miss Sasako?

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.330
Hey, isn't that mean?

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:06.090
It's you that I don't 
understand, Panda.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.640
What?

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:10.220
What do you think, Polar Bear?

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:13.400
Huh? Where's Polar Bear?

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:15.510
He's off today.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:19.170
Polar Bear goes out quite 
a bit, doesn't he?

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:22.330
He said there was something 
important he had to do today.

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.320
Something important?

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.820
Hibernating

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.900
Hibernating

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:05.030
Yes?

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:06.610
Hey!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.750
The hell do you want?!

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.440
What were you up to?

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:25.210
Hibernating

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:25.210
I was hibernating!

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:27.830
Oh, that's right.

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:30.890
You totally knew.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:31.910
Was it that obvious?

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.780
I'm going back to sleep now.

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:38.020
Then...

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.030
Let's go to the driving range.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:42.430
Go away!

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:47.980
Let's go! It's not good 
to do nothing but sleep.

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:50.300
That's what hibernating is!

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:55.880
Nice shot!

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.430
Damn it, I'm sleepy.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.580
The hell is this...

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:02.770
Grizzly.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.210
What?

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.840
Shouldn't you be asleep?

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.790
You're the one who woke me up!

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:10.800
Come on, no breaks!

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.690
Hurry up and hit!

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:15.380
I want to go home and sleep.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.130
Yeah, okay.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.500
Nice shot!

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.020
Come on, next!

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.490
All right, see you later.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.660
Oh, there they are.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.020
Hello!

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:37.860
Hey.

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:39.500
We're here!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.890
This is Grizzly.

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:43.270
We know.

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:45.540
This is Mr. Penguin and Panda.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.380
I know that. 
The hell are they doing here?

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.340
I think it's because I invited them.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:53.600
That's not what I meant!

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.470
<i>Why</i> did you invite them?!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.380
I thought you guys might want to see 
each other since it's been a while.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:01.350
I want to go home and see my pillow!

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.110
Well, your pillow isn't going anywhere,

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:05.520
so a little while with us won't hurt.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.290
All right? Let's all go together.

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:12.070
Where are we going, Mr. Grizzly?

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.200
Seems like I've got no other choice.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.330
Fine.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.800
What should we do now?

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.620
Let's see...

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:25.830
Take a walk?

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:30.210
Why would the four of us 
go for a walk at this hour?

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:33.090
Then let's go to Polar Bear's house.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.050
Oh, we can't.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:40.020
I'm drying kelp on the floor right now.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.280
There wouldn't be anywhere to step.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.190
What's with that?

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:48.070
If you're gonna make excuses, 
at least make them believable.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.490
So, what should we do?

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.360
Should we go somewhere?

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:56.000
I'm tired now.

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:58.320
Let's go eat.

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.040
What do you want to eat?

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.120
What are you in the
 mood for, Polar Bear?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.350
Anything is fine.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.450
I want to lay down.

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:09.980
What about sushi?

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.100
I'm not in the mood.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:14.640
You just said anything was fine.

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:17.540
What about your house, Polar Bear?

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:19.410
There's kelp on the floor.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:22.230
Yeah, yeah. Nowhere to step, right?

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:23.810
We got it.

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:27.730
Where should we go?

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:30.020
How about hot pot?!

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:33.480
I'll make the call.

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.900
Hello? There'll be four of us.

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:39.200
Be there in ten minutes.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.700
Hey, taxi!

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:44.580
Take this and go on ahead.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.460
I'll run there.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:51.420
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.900
Suigetsu Hot Pot

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.340
Cheers!

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:02.310
Come on, drink up!

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:07.480
Meat, shrimp, fish, 
shellfish, green onions!

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.280
All right!

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:11.480
This, too!

00:18:11.970 --> 00:18:14.160
Don't put in the garland 
chrysanthemum yet.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.900
Can I put in the tofu?

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.400
No, you can't!

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:22.370
All right. Now wait a while.

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:26.510
Did you have a job doing 
this before, Grizzly?

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.170
The hell do you mean a job?

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.460
You seem to know what you're doing.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.850
Why don't you close Grizzly's Bar

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:36.800
and open up a hot pot restaurant?

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:40.010
Shut up. I'm running the 
bar because I want to.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:41.890
Hey! What do you want to drink?

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:42.970
The same thing?

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:43.810
Yeah.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.700
Excuse me.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:49.470
Could we get a pitcher of 
beer and an orange juice?

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.860
That table's really demanding.

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:55.820
Don't touch it yet.

00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:06.450
All right.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:12.110
Tofu now!

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:12.820
Okay.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:15.550
Garland chrysanthemums, go!

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.010
Okay!

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:19.750
And it's done.

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:25.260
Here, Polar Bear.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.270
Thanks.

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:28.090
Panda!

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:29.800
Penguin!

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:31.560
Yay!

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:33.840
Now eat!

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:35.520
Thanks for the food.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:38.010
We're making porridge 
when you're done with that.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:39.320
So good.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:42.980
It's hot! I don't do well with hot.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.450
And now it's cooled off. 
Hurry up and eat.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:56.960
It's delicious! Thanks for everything!

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:00.540
More, please.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:06.800
Excuse me, could we get 
another pitcher of beer?

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:15.980
So, where are we going for round two?

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:20.170
Karaoke? A bar? Majority rules!

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:21.610
Karaoke!

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.100
What? You all want to go to a bar?

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.560
Come on, let's go.

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:30.340
Grizzly.

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.290
What?

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.960
I'm tired, so let's go home.

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:44.720
I got up early this morning, 
so I'm tired, too.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:49.740
It's okay... I can sleep anywhere...

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:50.930
Hey!

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.590
Don't sleep in the middle of the street!

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:58.010
I'll take you home. 
What the hell, you guys.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.400
Oh, hello, taxi?

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:05.410
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.500
Damn them.

00:21:14.180 --> 00:21:16.650
Why the hell did I take them home

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:18.200
when I'm supposed to be hibernating?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.410
The hell is this?

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:52.410
Jeez...

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:59.290
To Grizzly: 
Here's a pillow we all 
picked out for you.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:22:04.550
Goodnight. 
See you in the spring. 

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:01.760
Those guys are hopeless...

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:10.470
Goodnight. 
See you in the spring. 

00:23:54.870 --> 00:24:25.280
Next Time

00:23:58.130 --> 00:23:59.600
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:00.830
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:04.850
Have you done anything historically noteworthy lately, Mr. Penguin?

00:24:04.850 --> 00:24:06.900
I think you already 
know this, but no.

00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:08.380
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:09.720
Whoa!  Miss Sasako's voice!

00:24:09.720 --> 00:24:11.260
Where? Where is it coming from?!

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:12.680
Try to find me.

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:15.010
Isn't Miss Sasako's 
voice getting closer?

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:16.680
What is this, 
some kind of scary story?

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:18.310
Let's end this, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:19.310
Where are you?!

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:21.190
Next week's Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:22.470
will be presented putting safety first.

00:24:21.390 --> 00:24:24.590
Christmas Planning
Christmas Trouble

00:24:22.470 --> 00:24:23.280
Enjoy!

00:24:23.280 --> 00:24:24.570
Where are you?!
